NULLSCRIPT LICENSE

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to use,
copy, modify, and distribute the Software for personal, educational, hobby,
research, and nonprofit purposes.

Commercial use of software built with NullScript is permitted, provided that
NullScript itself is not used as a paid execution service.

---

PROHIBITED USES

The following uses are not permitted:

- Providing NullScript as a hosted execution service (including web apps, APIs,
  SaaS platforms, or cloud-based runners)
- Charging users for access to NullScript execution (including subscriptions,
  pay-per-run, API fees, or similar monetization models)
- Operating any service where the primary function is executing NullScript code
  submitted by users on infrastructure controlled by a third party
- Misrepresenting NullScript-based systems as something they are not (e.g.,
  labeling deterministic script execution systems as “AI” when they are not)

---

ALLOWED USES

The following uses are explicitly permitted:

- Running NullScript locally on any machine under user control
- Using VPS, cloud servers, containers, or remote environments to run NullScript,
  provided execution remains user-controlled and not sold as a service
- Using NullScript in general-purpose hosting platforms where it is only one
  tool among many
- Building and selling software created with NullScript (games, applications,
  tools, services), including monetization via sales, subscriptions, or ads
- Developing IDEs, editors, debuggers, and other developer tools that improve
  the NullScript experience
- Educational content, tutorials, and videos, including monetized content on
  third-party platforms (e.g., YouTube, Vimeo), provided they do not form a
  paid execution service for NullScript
- Sponsorships and advertising within educational content, provided they are
  reasonable and not designed as exploitative ad-extraction systems

---

ATTRIBUTION

Redistributions of the Software or substantial portions thereof must include
this license and appropriate attribution to the original NullScript project.

Attribution is encouraged for software built using NullScript where practical,
but is not required if the software is fully open-source or attribution is
already clearly visible in source materials.

---

EXECUTION PRINCIPLE

NullScript is intended to remain a locally-executable programming language.

It must always be possible for users to execute NullScript without requiring
payment, subscription, or remote authorization.

NullScript shall not be used as a hosted runtime product, API service, or
cloud execution platform.

